                     Part I — Additional Conditions

Definitions

For purposes of this License:

"Licensor" means Chih-Hung Chang (張誌宏), the individual who develops
and distributes Kumi and owns its copyright, and any successor or
assignee of that copyright.

"Kumi" means the software distributed by the Licensor under this
License, in Source or Object form, including its original code, compiled
code, documentation, configuration, and any Derivative Works of such
software.

"Your organization" means You, or the single legal entity on whose
behalf You exercise the permissions granted by this License, together
with any entities that control, are controlled by, or are under common
control with that entity, and the employees and individual contractors
of those entities when acting within their organizational roles.

For this definition, "control" means the direct or indirect power to
direct the management or policies of an entity, whether through
ownership, contract, or otherwise. External agencies, vendors, or
third-party companies engaged on a project or outsourcing basis are
separate entities and are not part of Your organization unless
controlled as defined above.

"Guest" means a person or entity outside Your organization whom You
invite into an instance of Kumi operated by Your organization to
collaborate with Your organization on Your organization's own specific
projects or activities.

"Operator" means a person or entity that operates, administers, or
controls a Kumi instance or service for the purpose of providing access
to Kumi to other persons or organizations. An organization that runs an
instance for its own use, including for its Guests, is not an Operator.
Merely providing infrastructure, installation, technical support, or
maintenance under the direction and control of the organization that
owns and uses the instance does not, by itself, make a service provider
an Operator.

"Kumi Interface" means any user interface that incorporates,
reproduces, or is derived in whole or in substantial part from the user
interface source code of Kumi. This includes, without limitation:

   - the source code located under the `web/` directory;
   - compiled or bundled web applications generated from that source
     code;
   - user interfaces included in Kumi container images or other builds;
   - modified, renamed, relocated, translated, or separately packaged
     versions of that interface code; and
   - derivative versions of the above.

A user interface independently developed without copying or deriving
from Kumi's protected interface code does not become a Kumi Interface
merely because it provides similar functionality, workflows, or visual
concepts.

"Substantial Part" means a portion of Kumi's Source or Object code, or
a modified, translated, compiled, or otherwise transformed version of
that code, that reproduces or incorporates a material portion of Kumi's
protected expression, core engine, workflow execution logic, data
models, or implementation. Whether a portion is substantial depends on
the qualitative nature and significance of the material used, not
merely on the percentage of code copied or whether the user interface
is omitted or replaced. Independent implementations of similar ideas,
functionality, protocols, or methods of operation are not considered
Substantial Parts solely because they provide similar capabilities.

"Commercial License" means a separate written permission granted by the
Licensor authorizing specific uses of Kumi that would otherwise be
restricted under Condition 2.

"Branding Waiver" means a separate written permission granted by the
Licensor authorizing specific removal, replacement, or modification of
Kumi branding that would otherwise be restricted under Condition 3.

A Commercial License and a Branding Waiver are separate permissions.
Either may be requested by contacting omar40276@gmail.com. A request
does not constitute permission. Permission is effective only when
expressly granted in writing by the Licensor.

Capitalized terms that Part I uses but does not define — including
"You", "Source", "Object", "Derivative Works", "Contribution" and
"Contributor" — have the meanings given in Part II. A reference to a
"Condition" is to a numbered condition of Part I. A reference to a
