8. Termination

   8(a). Automatic Termination

   If You engage in an activity that Condition 2 restricts without the
   required Commercial License, exceed the scope of a granted
   Commercial License, breach Condition 3, Condition 4, or
   Condition 7(d), or otherwise materially breach this License, the
   permissions granted to You under this License terminate
   automatically at the time of the breach. No notice from the Licensor
   is required.

   8(b). Reinstatement After Cure

   Your permissions are reinstated if You stop the breach and remedy it
   in full within thirty (30) days after the earlier of:

   1. the day You become aware of the breach; and
   2. the day You receive written notice of the breach from the
      Licensor.

   Reinstatement under this Condition 8(b) is available only for the
   first breach of which the Licensor notifies You. After any later
   breach, Your permissions are reinstated only under Condition 8(e).

   Reinstatement does not waive any claim, fee, or remedy that the
   Licensor has for the period during which the breach continued.

   8(c). Effect of Termination

   Upon termination, and for as long as Your permissions are not
   reinstated:

   1. You must immediately cease all activities that require
      permissions under this License;
   2. You must stop operating any unauthorized hosted or managed Kumi
      service;
   3. You must stop distributing Kumi in any manner that requires
      permissions You no longer hold;
   4. any continued use, reproduction, hosting, or distribution of Kumi
      without valid permissions constitutes both a breach of this
      License and copyright infringement, entitling the Licensor to
      injunctive relief, damages, and all other remedies available under
      applicable law; and
   5. any outstanding obligations accrued before termination remain
      enforceable.

   8(d). Downstream Recipients

   Termination of Your permissions does not automatically terminate the
   permissions previously granted to recipients who received Kumi or a
   Derivative Work from You in compliance with this License, provided
   that those recipients continue to comply with the applicable license
   terms.

   8(e). Reinstatement by the Licensor

   The Licensor may reinstate terminated permissions through an express
   written authorization. Reinstatement is effective only within the
   scope specified in that authorization.

